<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kikkawa clan</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kikkawa were a Japanese warrior clan of Aki province, in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/honshu">Honshu</a>. In the 16th century Mōri Motonari placed his son Motoharu at its head, and with the Kobayakawa it became one of the 'two rivers' supporting the Mōri. At <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-sekigahara">Sekigahara</a> in 1600 Kikkawa Hiroie stayed out of the fighting after secret talks with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokugawa-ieyasu">Tokugawa Ieyasu</a>, and his descendants ruled the Iwakuni domain throughout the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edo-period">Edo period</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kikkawa-clan.jpg" alt="Kikkawa clan" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Horlicks (talk · contribs), vectorized by Fvasconcellos (talk · contribs) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Marunouchinimitsuhikiryo.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
